1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,994
Substituents tune the acidity.

2
00:00:02,994 --> 00:00:18,111
Electron withdrawing nitro groups pull charge away from the phenoxide ion and stabilise it, so para nitrophenol is stronger, and picric acid, with three nitro groups, is almost as strong as a mineral acid.

3
00:00:18,111 --> 00:00:25,260
An electron releasing methyl group does the opposite: para cresol is slightly weaker than phenol.

